  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all incidents and 72-hour customer notice with no investigation delay. S2 keeps the 55°C test and 5% threshold but makes exceedance a corrective-action trigger rather than an automatic sales ban, with customer access to numeric rates but no public disclosure. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a six-year retrofit deadline with an equivalent-measure escape. S4 requires built-in fire suppression at 36 months. S5 mandates recall above 8 incidents/100k with prompt customer notices but no serious-injury clause."
